    "field": "Coupled climate modeling",
    "problem": "Coupled climate models are limited because increasing ocean resolution without a corresponding increase in atmospheric resolution fails to properly realize important feedback effects, as the coarser atmosphere cannot resolve the fine-scale oceanic features that are generated.",
    "method": "The paper proposes a method of concurrently increasing atmospheric and oceanic model resolution within a coupled framework to properly simulate key climate processes and feedbacks that are misrepresented when only one component\u2019s resolution is improved.",
    "task": "The task is to analyze the impact of relative atmosphere and ocean model resolution on coupled climate models by comparing a matrix of simulations to determine how resolution affects the representation of key ocean-atmosphere interactions.",
